================================================================
OSI Model (7 Layers)
================================================================
Mnemonic: All People Seem To Need Data Processing
(Top → Bottom)



================================================================
7. Application
================================================================

👉 What users & applications interact with

Examples: HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, SMTP, DNS

This is where your browser, curl, Postman live

Deals with requests, responses, APIs

🔹 If a website isn’t loading → start thinking here


================================================================
6. Presentation
================================================================
👉 Data formatting, encryption, compression

Examples:

SSL/TLS encryption

JSON ↔ XML ↔ binary

Makes sure data is readable by the application

🔹 HTTPS encryption happens here

================================================================
5. Session
================================================================
👉 Session management

Establishes, maintains, terminates sessions

Authentication sessions, checkpoints, re-connects

🔹 “Are we still connected?” layer


================================================================
4. Transport
================================================================

👉 End-to-end communication & reliability

Protocols: TCP, UDP

Handles:

Ports (80, 443, 5432)

Flow control

Retransmission

🔹 TCP handshake (SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK) happens here

================================================================
3. Network
================================================================

👉 Routing & IP addressing

Protocols: IP, ICMP

Devices: Routers

Decides best path to destination

🔹 ping, traceroute → Layer 3


================================================================
2. Data Link
================================================================

👉 MAC addresses & local delivery

Ethernet, ARP

Devices: Switches

Frames data for physical transmission

🔹 ARP: “Who has this IP? Tell me your MAC”

================================================================
1. Physical
================================================================
👉 Actual bits on the wire

Cables, fiber, voltages, NICs

0s and 1s

🔹 Broken cable = Layer 1 issue


================================================================
Quick DevOps / Troubleshooting Mapping
================================================================
Problem	Likely Layer
Cable unplugged	Layer 1
ARP not resolving	Layer 2
No route to host	Layer 3
Port blocked / firewall	Layer 4
Session drops	Layer 5
SSL cert error	Layer 6
500 / API error	Layer 7


================================================================
Real-World Example: Accessing a Website
================================================================
Layer 7 – Browser sends HTTP request

Layer 6 – Encrypts using TLS

Layer 5 – Session established

Layer 4 – TCP ensures delivery

Layer 3 – IP routing

Layer 2 – MAC resolution

Layer 1 – Bits sent over cable
